U/Sections: 420, 406 BNS, 2023 (Corresponding to Sections 420, 406 IPC)

APPLICATION UNDER SECTION 483 BHARATIYA NAGARIK SURAKSHA SANHITA, 2023
(READ WITH SECTION 439 CrPC) FOR GRANT OF REGULAR BAIL

MOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:

1. That the Applicant has been falsely implicated in the present FIR registered at the instance of disgruntled private investors following commercial trading losses incurred in turbulent commodity and stock markets.

2. That the Applicant is in judicial custody since 15.06.2025. The investigation is complete and the Chargesheet has already been filed on 01.07.2025. Custodial interrogation is no longer required.

3. That the dispute is purely civil in character. The investments were made pursuant to signed Joint Venture and Profit-Sharing Agreements wherein market volatility risks were explicitly agreed upon by all participants.

4. That the Applicant has never had any dishonest intention at the inception of the transaction. Over ₹45 lakhs has already been disbursed back to investors prior to market crash as documented in bank ledger statements.

5. That all books of account, bank accounts, and servers have been seized by the Investigating Agency; hence there is zero risk of evidence tampering.

6. That the Applicant is a permanent resident of Udaipur with deep social roots and undertakes to abide by any stringent bail conditions, including surrender of passport and periodic reporting.

PRAYER:
It is therefore respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to release the Applicant on regular bail during the pendency of trial, on such terms and conditions as deemed fit.

Applicant / Advocate for Applicant
Verified at Udaipur on this 15th day of July, 2025.
